    {
      "id": "r20261030-a02",
      "title": "How Video Games Are Helping Hospitals",
      "level": "Menengah atas",
      "min": 4,
      "body": [
        "Video games are often blamed for making children lazy, but hospitals around the world are finding surprising ways to use them for good.",
        "In some children's hospitals, young patients play special games during painful treatments. The games distract them, so they feel less pain and need less medicine. In other hospitals, games help patients recover movement after injuries. Moving a character on the screen becomes exercise for weak arms and legs, and because it feels like play, patients practice longer.",
        "Doctors say games are not a magic cure, and screen time still needs limits. But when a game can turn a difficult treatment into something a child does not fear, it becomes a useful medical tool. Sometimes, play is serious medicine."
      ],
      "gloss": {
        "blamed": "disalahkan",
        "patients": "pasien",
        "treatments": "perawatan",
        "distract": "mengalihkan",
        "recover": "memulihkan",
        "injuries": "cedera",
        "limits": "batasan",
        "cure": "obat"
      },
      "qs": [
        {
          "q": "How do games help children during painful treatments?",
          "opts": [
            "They distract them from the pain",
            "They make treatments shorter",
            "They replace all medicine"
          ],
          "a": 0
        },
        {
